        <!-- IMPORTANT, and not obvious: a per-device build (monkeyc -d <id>) only
             ever loads the one definition it was pointed at, so it cannot tell you
             anything about the other ids in here - a typo sits in this file
             indefinitely and surfaces only when the store package is exported. The
             'Invalid device id found in the application manifest' warning, which
             also does not distinguish a nonexistent id from a definition you have
             simply not installed, was not observed at all on SDK 9.2.0.

             Because of that, this list is not hand-written: every id here is a
             filename in the SDK's own device reference
             (Sdks/<sdk>/doc/docs/Device_Reference/<id>.html), which is what makes
             them real rather than plausible. The filter applied was:

               - wrist-worn (Edge, GPSMAP, Montana, Oregon, Rino and eTrex dropped);
               - declares the Watch App type (drops fr45 and garminswim2, which are
                 watch-face only);
               - declares the Background type, which arrived in Connect IQ 2.4 and
                 so is a proxy for satisfying minSdkVersion above. That is what
                 drops fenix3, epix (gen 1), vivoactive (gen 1), fr230/235/630/920xt
                 and the D2 Bravo pair.

             124 devices survive. Re-run that filter against a newer SDK to extend
             the list; do not add ids by hand.

             Layout note: the view handles round and semi-octagon deliberately (see
             ShakeDetectorLayout.mc). The 6 rectangle devices (Venu Sq family, Venu
             X1, vivoactive HR) and semi-round fr735xt render with the round
             geometry, which is legible but not tuned. -->
